My method, which is a little more work but probably safer, is to call
an unidentified potion "bad" just before dipping my unicorn horn into
it.  If I just get "Interesting..." I get rid of the call (call it " ").
If it does clear, the next time I find the same type of potion, it 
will be called "bad" and it will be obvious that I already tested it.

I use a similar method for gems, calling any soft gems "glass" just 
before putting them in a chest and kicking.  Any that survive I 
call "val".
